  "title": "Places in town and directions",
  "note": "Going to a place: do + genitive (idę do sklepu, do banku, do apteki). Being there: w + locative (w sklepie, w banku, w aptece). Some places take na instead: idę na pocztę (accusative), jestem na poczcie (locative). Masculine genitive often ends in -u for places (sklepu, parku) and -a for people (do brata).",
  "src": {"t": "Polish grammar: genitive and locative, Wikipedia", "u": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polish_grammar"},
